;;;; src/evops.lisp — x86-64 assembly for the encoder's hot loops (SBCL).
;;;;
;;;; As in src/dvops.lisp (see its header for the ST/CTX protocol and why
;;;; no pinning is needed): a speed path only.  Each routine reproduces a
;;;; Lisp loop of src/encode.lisp exactly - same table updates, same
;;;; commands, same bits - so the output does not depend on whether the
;;;; assembly ran, and the Lisp loop stays the code for other
;;;; implementations.
;;;;
;;;; Bit writer: BWR's POS / ACC / NBITS in registers; a write ORs
;;;; BITS << NBITS into ACC (writes are <= 32 bits), and once 32 bits are
;;;; pending the 8-byte ACC is stored at POS and POS advances 4 bytes.  The
;;;; caller converts back to BWR's NBITS < 8 form, and guarantees room for
;;;; every byte the routine may write.
